TASK: Fix the slow image attachment UX in BlueMind chat.

CURRENT PROBLEM:
After selecting photos and tapping “Add”, the app returns to the chat but the images take noticeable time before appearing inside the composer.

The user should NOT wait for upload/processing before seeing the selected images.

==================================================
DESIRED BEHAVIOR
==================================================

Use an optimistic local preview flow.

Immediately after the user taps Add:

1. close the media sheet
2. render the selected images INSIDE the composer immediately
3. use local image URIs / object URLs / native asset previews
4. start upload/compression in the background
5. replace/update the local attachment state with the uploaded asset only after upload completes

The UI must not wait for:
- server upload
- base64 conversion
- cloud response
- remote URL generation

before showing the thumbnail.

==================================================
IMPORTANT
==================================================

Do NOT block composer rendering on upload completion.

Do NOT do:
select image
-> convert full image
-> upload
-> wait for server URL
-> then render thumbnail

Instead do:
select image
-> create instant local preview
-> render immediately
-> upload asynchronously

==================================================
PERFORMANCE
==================================================

For preview:
- use a lightweight local thumbnail
- do not decode/render the full-resolution image for the composer preview
- generate or request a smaller preview size if supported
- avoid converting large photos to huge base64 strings on the main thread

If compression is needed:
- perform it asynchronously
- do not block UI
- preserve original file for upload if necessary

==================================================
UPLOAD STATE
==================================================

Each attachment should have a state such as:

local
uploading
uploaded
failed

While uploading:
- keep the image visible
- optionally show a very subtle spinner/progress indicator on the thumbnail
- user can continue typing

On success:
- remove spinner
- keep same thumbnail position

On failure:
- show retry indicator
- do not make image disappear silently

==================================================
MULTIPLE PHOTOS
==================================================

For 2, 3, 4+ selected photos:

All thumbnails should appear immediately together inside the composer.

Do not wait sequentially for each upload.

Start uploads concurrently with a reasonable concurrency limit.

Preserve photo selection order.

==================================================
COMPOSER
==================================================

The composer must expand immediately when attachments are confirmed.

No blank delay.
No layout jump several seconds later.

Expected:
Tap Add 2
-> sheet closes
-> both thumbnails are already visible inside composer within ~100–200ms
-> uploads continue in background

==================================================
IPHONE PERFORMANCE CHECK
==================================================

Test on a physical iPhone with:
- 1 photo
- 2 photos
- 5 photos
- large high-resolution camera photos

Measure:
- time from tapping Add to thumbnail appearing
- upload time separately

Target:
UI preview should feel instant even if actual upload takes several seconds.

==================================================
DO NOT CHANGE
==================================================

Do not redesign:
- composer
- media sheet
- selection UI
- message bubble layout

Only improve attachment loading/rendering performance.

At the end report:
- what was causing the delay
- whether base64/full-resolution decoding was blocking UI
- how local previews are generated
- how uploads run in background
- measured Add-to-preview time on physical iPhone
